      This command will re-display the last command that you entered that was
      at least five characters in length.
@X0F
   Description
@X03
      Sometimes you may want to re-display the last command that you entered
      so that you can execute it again.  From the Conference Command prompt,
      you can use this command to re-display the last command that you
      executed that was at least five characters in length.  In the long run,
      this could save you a lot of typing.  This command is almost identical
      to pressing F3 while at a DOS prompt.
@X0F
   Examples
@X03
      Enter the following to search for the words PCBOARD and LAN:
    @X0E
           TS 1+ PCBOARD & LAN
@X03
      Now join another conference:
@X0E
           J 1
@X03
      And repeat the last command issued which was 5 characters or longer:
@X0E
           !
@X03
      After pressing ENTER the following will be displayed which you can
      then modify or press ENTER to accept:
@X0E
           TS 1+ PCBOARD & LAN
